==Historical party systems==

===The "Saito System" (1890–1940)===
Following the promulgation of the [[Saito Constitution]] in 1889, Okaiken developed a competitive party system centered on the [[Imperial Diet]]. The [[Rikken Seiyūkai]] dominated this period, representing landlord interests and the established bureaucracy. The [[Kenseitō]] and later [[Kenseikai]] and [[Rikken Minseitō]] served as liberal opposition forces advocating for expanded democratic rights.

This system collapsed in 1940 with the formation of the [[Taisei Yokusankai]], which absorbed all political parties into a single state apparatus during the militarist period.

===The "Post-War System" (1950–1968)===
Following the [[Great Adonian War]], the [[Okaiken Democratic Party]] emerged as the dominant conservative force, governing from 1956 until merging into the [[Republican Party]] in 1966. The Republican Party then dominated the [[Federal Republic of Okaiken|Republican era]], governing from 1968 until the formation of the Liberal Democratic Party in 1977.

During this period, the [[Sanese Communist Party]] and [[Okaiken Socialist Party]] served as permanent opposition parties. The OSP briefly held the premiership under [[Genzui Kusaka]] (1966–1968), whose government's attempts to abolish parliament triggered the [[Quiet Revolution]] of 1968.

===The "1977 System" (1977–2016)===
From the founding of the Liberal Democratic Party in 1977 until its electoral collapse in 2016, Okaiken operated under a dominant-party system. The LDP governed continuously for 39 years, interrupted only briefly from 1990 to 1993 when a multi-party coalition led by the Progressive Party held power.

During this period, the '''LDP''' was the dominant conservative force, overseeing the "Go-go 8090" economic boom and navigating the "Lost Decades" that followed. The '''Progressive Party (PPO)''' served as the primary opposition, briefly governing from 1990 to 1993 under [[Shigehara Honda]]. The '''Sanese Communist Party (SCP)''' and '''Okaiken Socialist Party (OSP)''' were minor opposition parties, with the OSP banned from 1968 to 1988 following the Quiet Revolution.

===The "2016 Realignment" (2016–present)===
The 2016 general election shattered the 1977 System. The LDP collapsed following the resignation of [[Toshiro Kurosawa]] and the [[Data-Gate scandal]], while the SCP surged to a historic victory under [[Sho Aoyagi]].

Key developments include the '''2016''' election where SCP won 138 seats, forming the first communist-led government in Okaiken history while the LDP collapsed to 88 seats. In '''2021''', the PPO under [[Honda Shigetsuma]] won 201 seats, becoming the largest party, while the SCP fell to 90 seats. The '''2025''' election saw the OSP surge from 2 seats to 50 under [[Rento Nakayama]], while the LDP gained 40 seats and the SCP collapsed to 45 seats following the "Parasite gaffe."

